Service

What is a Kubernetes Service

	In Kubernetes, a Service is an object that exposes a group of Pods and provides a stable network endpoint to access them.

Pods in Kubernetes are temporary (ephemeral):

	Pods can restart

	Pods can get new IP addresses

	Pods can be rescheduled to different nodes

	A Service solves this problem by providing:

		Stable IP address

		Stable DNS name

service Types
=============
1. ClusterIP
2. NodePort
3. Load balancer


Why We Use Kubernetes Services

Without Service:

	Client → Pod1 (IP: 10.1.1.5)

If Pod restarts:

	Pod1 → new IP (10.1.3.9)
	Client connection breaks 

with service 

	Client
	   ↓
	Service (ClusterIP)
	   ↓
	Pod1
	Pod2
	Pod3

Benefits:

	Stable IP
	Load balancing
	Service discovery
	Decoupling between pods

